                <pb facs="0367" n="358" sameAs="frus:frus1938v05/pg358"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.5151/1213: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-10-14T17:00:00-03:00">October 14, 1938—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 14—5 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>242. Aranha told me today confidentially that in his opinion the only way to
                    solve the present exchange difficulties is to remove all exchange restrictions.
                    If this were done, he said, he would insist that the German mark be treated in
                    the same fashion that other currencies are treated. He said that the matter is
                    being given serious consideration in Government circles but admitted that it is
                    meeting with considerable opposition.</p>
                <p>Please inform Department of Commerce.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
